From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rdkb-cli: place clients inside expanded SSID bubbles

The topology drew every STA on a ring around the whole EasyMesh device.  With
separate private and IoT cohorts this made the SSID color bubbles decorative:
the viewer still had to follow a line or open a tooltip to learn which cohort
owned a client.

Make private_ssid and iot_ssid circles larger and space all haul circles a bit
further apart.  Place every station deterministically inside the circle whose
SSID matches its authoritative topology record.  A golden-angle disk layout
uses the available area more evenly than one perimeter ring and reduces icon
size gradually for future larger cohorts.  Use the resulting node extent for
D3 collision spacing so expanded groups do not overlap adjacent Agents.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lab WebUI presentation]
